# GUIShop Worth Display System

The worth display system shows item sell values in the item lore, updated in real-time via packets.

## Requires
- **PacketEvents** library (optional dependency)
- Enabled in `worth.yml`

## Key Classes

### WorthDisplayManager (`src/com/pablo67340/guishop/worth/`)
- Manages packet listeners for worth lore injection
- Handles SET_SLOT and WINDOW_ITEMS packets
- Modifies item lore client-side only (no server-side changes)

### Worth Configuration (`worth.yml`)
```yaml
enabled: true
format: "&7Worth: &a$%worth%"
hide-armor-slots: true  # Don't show worth on equipped armor
inventory-title-blacklist:  # Inventories to skip
  - "Auction House"
  - "Crate"
item-name-blacklist:  # Items with these name patterns get no worth
  - "Backpack"
  - "Kit"
```

## How It Works

1. **Packet Interception:**
   - Listens for SET_SLOT and WINDOW_ITEMS packets
   - Modifies items BEFORE sending to client

2. **Worth Lookup:**
   - Checks `GUIShop.getITEMTABLE()` for sell price
   - Uses item material + optional NBT matching

3. **Lore Injection:**
   - Appends worth line to existing lore
   - Only visual (client-side), original item unchanged

## API Hook

Other plugins can disable worth for specific players:
```java
GUIShopAPI.setExternalWorthCheck(player -> {
    return myPlugin.hasWorthDisabled(player);
});
```

## Player Toggle Command
```
/gs toggleworth - Toggles worth display for the player (session only)
```

## Common Issues

**Worth not showing:**
- Check PacketEvents is installed
- Check `worth.yml` enabled: true
- Check item is registered in ITEMTABLE (has sell price in shop)

**Worth showing in wrong inventories:**
- Add inventory title to blacklist in worth.yml

**Worth on equipped armor:**
- Set `hide-armor-slots: true` in worth.yml
